TAR››tar c archive.tar file ...›tar t archive.tar›tar v archive.tar›tar x archive.tar››Creates, lists and extracts›uncompressed POSIX USTAR archives.›Creation uses›one 512-byte streaming buffer, exact›EOSFS names, mode 0644, uid/gid zero›and›the EOSFS timestamp. Files and›directory trees are archived›recursively to a›maximum depth of 16. Two zero blocks›terminate the archive.››t lists names. v lists sizes and›names. x creates directory entries and›extracts regular files, restoring›representable timestamps while›ignoring›Unix ownership and permissions.›Existing files are reported and never›overwritten; existing directories are›reused explicitly.››The reader accepts POSIX USTAR and V7›headers. Extraction rejects absolute›paths, device paths, parent traversal,›overlong names, malformed octal›fields,›bad checksums, truncated archives and›unsupported member types. Names are›never silently truncated.››There is no compression in this›version. Use Toolkit arc only for›legacy›SEA ARC files.›